{
  "_comment": "Devin hook payloads RE-MEASURED 2026-10-05 with a stdin-capture hook on every event in a trusted workspace, on Devin CLI 3000.6.12 and 3000.11.3 (the CLI self-updated mid-capture; the shapes agree). Every KEY and nesting is as delivered; ids and paths are anonymized and long text is shortened. This corrects the 2026-09-02 corpus, which had write/edit/read keyed on `path` (live: `file_path`), edit on `old_str`/`new_str` (live: `old_string`/`new_string`), todo_write as `{status, activeForm}` (live: `{todos: [{content, status}]}`), run_subagent as `{profile, prompt}` (live: `{title, task, profile, is_background}`), and an `agent_type` on the run_subagent result (live: none). Every tool_response is an object `{success, output, error}`; a refused spawn still fires PostToolUse with `success: false`. No payload carries `cwd` or `transcript_path`. Not captured live (the default model was not offered the tool, or no event occurred): apply_patch, notebook_read, notebook_edit, postCompaction. Those entries keep Claude-shaped inputs and are marked `_shape: \"not-captured\"`.",
